  "notes": "The R&B-hook end of the Memphis spectrum, and the second Suave House entry — so like 8Ball & MJG it overrides the parent's harmony rather than tightening it: minor-7 and dominant-9 voicings with ii–v–i and i–iv motion, **real changes rather than drones**. What separates him from the duo is softness rather than harmony. The research says the 808 kit carries soul-record swing, that fills are **keyboard-led rather than snare-roll-led**, and that hats are 8ths with light 16th accents — so `session.swing` rises to 0.60 (the loosest in this batch), the hat-roll frequency sits at the bottom of its band and the snare roll is the gappiest of the Suave House pair. The played bass line walks the changes, hence `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.55 with four passing tones. The keyboard countermelody between vocal phrases is a described part, so it runs at 0.5 density with `fillGapsOnly` on — it fills the gaps, which is literally what \"between vocal phrases\" means, and it is the only entry here using `arp` alongside the answer lick. ⚠ `low`: the research rates it medium-low and says **the harmony and drum values are inherited from the documented Suave House / 8Ball & MJG template rather than sourced for him**, and marks the tempo band [LOW-CONF] (66–78 half-time = 132–156 straight). The label, the era and the hit single are what is sourced; `chords`, `drums.kick` and `session.bpm` are the inferred blocks. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 47 to 45 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 46 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 2.",
